  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/940a6996800ee85745643b34e429bb1fa85064bbab94f52bed328b074024fd22.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides.",
  "worked_solution": "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{⟷}{EA}$ and  $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$ are perpendicular.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/81e84f9f6f3f50f6a5ef3f39381ebce028ccb52fa09b2d7042c9206a7027f337.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{EA}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ are perpendicular. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{EA}⊥\\overset{―}{AB}\n$$",
